import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'brand':('The brand need that counted twice',
  'A level fifty druid wields a long bow - shooter power three - wears a firebrand ring, and carries five identified plain arrows. The brand-the-ammo test appeared twice in the inventory scan with the same condition, so the single qualifying stack added twenty to the need-brand trait instead of ten. The correction keeps the copy that sits with the enchant logic: ten.'),
 'control':('Control: a stack too small to brand',
  'The same druid and bow with only two arrows, below the five the test requires: the need stays zero before and after, and the complete log is byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/brand-240 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag in ('RATING ','OUTCOME '):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[tag.split()[0].lower()]=match[1].strip() if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The brand need that counted twice</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native brand-need readings</p><h1>The brand need that counted twice</h1><p>The Borg tracks how much it needs to brand its ammunition as a trait that feeds its shopping and preparation thinking. The brand-the-ammo test was pasted twice into the inventory scan - once inside the good-shooter block and once after it, with the same condition - so every qualifying stack counted double.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">Need value</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the control establishes</h2><p>A stack of two arrows, below the five the test requires, leaves the need at zero in both variants with byte-identical logs: the correction removes only the duplicated test.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Druid level fifty, depth thirty, seed one thousand, lit constructed arena, every class book carried, a long bow wielded (shooter power three), a firebrand ring worn as the brand ability, five (or two, in the control) identified plain arrows. The measurement reads the need-brand trait after one inventory scan. This isolates the duplicated test, not full autonomous play. No death or survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/240">issue240</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);let r=d.rating||'';let m=r.match(/need_brand=(-?\\d+)/);p.querySelector('.num').textContent='Need value: '+(m?m[1]:'n/a');p.querySelector('.state').textContent=d.outcome||'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='brand'?'The original counts the single qualifying stack twice (20 against the correction 10).':'Too small to brand: zero either way, byte for byte.';}select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
